  id: W2_06
  era: Late 5th century CE
  title: Padmapani, Ajanta Cave 1
  text: Padmapani, Ajanta Cave 1. About thirty Buddhist caves were cut into a horseshoe-shaped cliff at Ajanta between the 2nd century BCE and the late 5th century CE. This bodhisattva of compassion, holding a lotus, is one of the most celebrated wall paintings of Cave 1. The caves were abandoned and forgotten for centuries until a British officer, John Smith, stumbled on them while hunting a tiger in 1819.
